  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p data-sourcepos=&quot;7:1-7:358&quot;&gt;Prior to the first operation of the condenser units hereby approved&amp;nbsp;a signed contractual agreement for the cleaning and maintenance schedule of the extract and odour control system must be submitted to and approved in writing by the Council. The approved schedule must be implemented before the first operation and maintained for the lifetime of the use.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-sourcepos=&quot;9:1-9:158&quot;&gt;REASON: To ensure the amenity of occupiers of the development site and surrounding premises is not adversely affected by smell, steam, and other effluent.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Within three months of installation, a post-installation photographic evidence shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority for approval, demonstrating that the proposal has been installed correctly as approved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reason: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers and the surrounding area.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The noise level from all plant and machinery included in the approved development shall at all times remain 5dB(A) below background levels when measured at any nearby residential window or other sensitive receptor if appropriate (add/delete as appropriate)\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that occupiers of neighbouring premises do not suffer a loss of amenity by reason of noise nuisance and other excess noise.\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;The operation of any building services plant hereby approved shall not\r\ncommence until &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;i. a post-installation noise assessment has been carried out to confirm\r\ncompliance with the noise criteria, and the results shall be submitted to the local planning authority for approval. The scheme shall be implemented in accordance\r\nwith the approved details and attenuation measures, and they shall be permanently\r\nretained and maintained in working order for the duration of the use and their\r\noperation; and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;ii. a post-installation sound insulation test&amp;nbsp;shall be carried out to determine that adequate sound insulation has been provided to limit egress noise to the dwelling above the commercial unit, and the results submitted to the local planning authority for approval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To protect the amenities of adjoining occupiers and the surrounding area.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
